From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Sotraidis <56282582+chrissotraidis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 23:41:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] port: do not walk a GL inventory that was never created

Delete() walks the 16 per-level containers, their lists and their AVL
trees, and Create() is what builds all of them.  The global glInventory is
constructed as a static object, so its destructor runs on every exit path,
including the ones that end the process before the renderer exists -- a bad
STRIKERS_BACKEND= name returning 1 from main, and now the unresolved-disc
refusal that the entry point reports.  Unguarded, ReleaseLevel() dereferences
a null m_pFileData[nLevel] and the process dies of SIGSEGV during
__cxa_finalize instead of exiting with the status it chose.

Measured before the change: STRIKERS_BACKEND=zzz exits 139 with the crash in
GLInventory::Delete, on the same binary where a valid disc exits 0.  After,
both exit with their own status and no signal handler runs.

m_bCreated is the flag Create() and Delete() already keep for this question,
so the guard adds no new state.

// PORT: a crash on the way out of a failed start; no behaviour change to a run
// that reaches Create().
---
 smstrikers-port/src/Game/GL/GLInventory.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smstrikers-port/src/Game/GL/GLInventory.cpp b/smstrikers-port/src/Game/GL/GLInventory.cpp
index b478e7e..287e177 100644
--- a/smstrikers-port/src/Game/GL/GLInventory.cpp
+++ b/smstrikers-port/src/Game/GL/GLInventory.cpp
@@ -26,7 +26,13 @@ GLInventory glInventory;
  */
 GLInventory::~GLInventory()
 {
-    Delete();
+    // PORT: Delete() walks the per-level containers and their trees, and Create() is what builds
+    // them. A process that ends before the renderer is up -- no disc, a host whose importer has not
+    // run yet, a bad backend name -- still runs this destructor, and unguarded it segfaults in
+    // ReleaseLevel() on a null container instead of exiting with its own status. m_bCreated is the
+    // flag Create() and Delete() already keep for exactly this question.
+    if (m_bCreated)
+        Delete();
 }
 
